>
  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="cost">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>How much does central heating installation cost in St Helens?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">A full new system starts from £4,495 for a 2-bed home, £5,295 for a 3-bed and £6,295 for a 4-bed, including VAT. A combi conversion starts from £2,890.</p>
      <div class="brx-table-wrap">
        <table class="brx-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Home</th><th>Typical radiators</th><th>Price, inc VAT</th><th>Typical time</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><strong>2-bed flat or house</strong></td><td>Up to 6</td><td>from £4,495</td><td>2 to 3 days</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>3-bed terrace or semi</strong></td><td>7 to 10</td><td>from £5,295</td><td>4 to 5 days</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>4-bed house</strong></td><td>11 or more</td><td>from £6,295</td><td>5 to 7 days</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Combi conversion</strong></td><td>Keeps your radiators</td><td>from £2,890</td><td>1 to 2 days</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>The price depends on the number of radiators, the pipe runs and the boiler you choose. A back boiler adds work, as the fire comes out and the boiler moves. That is why we visit first. The survey is free, and the price is fixed and in writing.</p>
      <p>Need just one more radiator? See our <a href="/radiators-st-helens">St Helens radiator prices</a>, from £245 supplied and fitted.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="back-boilers">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Do you replace back boilers in St Helens?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Yes. Back boilers are still common in older St Helens homes, and replacing them is one of our most common jobs here. We remove the old one and fit a modern combi.</p>
      <p>A back boiler sits behind a gas fire in the chimney breast. Many terraces in WA10 and WA9 still have one. They are old, parts are hard to find, and they waste gas. We do not service them. We replace them.</p>
      <h3>What does a back boiler replacement involve?</h3>
      <ul class="sg-ticks">
        <li><strong>Fire and back boiler out.</strong> We remove them together and cap the old gas supply.</li>
        <li><strong>Opening made good.</strong> The chimney breast opening is left safe and tidy.</li>
        <li><strong>New boiler position.</strong> In most WA10 terraces it goes in the kitchen or a downstairs cupboard.</li>
        <li><strong>New gas pipe and pipework.</strong> Old back boiler pipes rarely reach the best radiator spots.</li>
        <li><strong>New radiators</strong> where the old ones are worn or in the wrong place.</li>
        <li><strong>Clean, fill and balance.</strong> Old pipes often hold sludge, so we clean the system well.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>It is a bigger job than a boiler swap. With new radiators it usually takes 4 to 5 days. We plan it all at the free survey.</p>
      <div class="brx-cta">
        <p><strong>Still on a back boiler?</strong> Book a free survey for a fixed written price.</p>
        <a href={TEL} class="brx-btn">Call {PHONE}</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="options">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Which option is right for my St Helens home?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">It depends on what you have now. Not every home needs a whole new system. We tell you honestly at the survey.</p>
      <div class="sg-cols">
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>A full new system</h3>
          <p>Best if you have a back boiler with old pipes, no central heating, or only electric heaters. From £4,495.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>A combi conversion</h3>
          <p>Best if you have a hot water cylinder and loft tanks. We fit a combi and keep sound radiators. From £2,890.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-cols" style="margin-top:1rem;">
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>A new boiler only</h3>
          <p>Best if your radiators and pipes work well. See <a href="/boiler-installation-st-helens">boiler installation in St Helens</a> from £2,195.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>An upgrade</h3>
          <p>Best if some rooms are cold. An extra radiator or a <a href="/power-flushing-st-helens">power flush</a> may be all you need.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <h3>Signs your home needs new central heating</h3>
      <ul class="sg-ticks">
        <li><strong>You still have a back boiler</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Rooms stay cold</strong> with the heating on</li>
        <li><strong>Cold spots</strong> on radiators that bleeding does not fix</li>
        <li><strong>High bills</strong> for little heat</li>
        <li><strong>A poor EPC rating</strong> of D or lower</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="included">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>What is included in a new central heating system?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Everything you need for a working system. There are no hidden extras.</p>
      <ul class="sg-ticks">
        <li><strong>New A-rated boiler</strong> from Baxi, Worcester Bosch or Vaillant, sized for your home</li>
        <li><strong>Back boiler and fire removal</strong> where you have one</li>
        <li><strong>New radiators</strong>, each sized for its room, with TRVs</li>
        <li><strong>All new pipework</strong>, routed to keep it out of sight where we can</li>
        <li><strong>Smart or programmable controls</strong>, set up and shown to you</li>
        <li><strong>Magnetic filter, system clean and inhibitor</strong> to BS 7593</li>
        <li><strong>Balancing</strong>, so every room heats evenly</li>
        <li><strong>Gas safety checks and Benchmark</strong> filled in on the day</li>
        <li><strong>12-month workmanship guarantee</strong> on all our work</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Want a smart thermostat that needs new wiring? Our partner firm <a href="https://www.idealelectricalsolutions.co.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ideal Electrical Solutions</a> does the electrical work.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="time">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>How long does central heating installation take in St Helens?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">A small home takes 2 to 3 days. A back boiler job or a 3-bed system takes 4 to 5 days. Bigger homes in Haydock or Newton-le-Willows can take 5 to 7 days.</p>
      <ol class="sg-steps">
        <li><strong>Free survey.</strong> We check the layout, the existing system, the walls and the best boiler spot. You get a fixed written price.</li>
        <li><strong>Day 1: strip out.</strong> We cover floors, drain down and remove the fire and back boiler.</li>
        <li><strong>Days 2 and 3: pipes and radiators.</strong> We run new pipes and hang the new radiators.</li>
        <li><strong>Day 4: boiler.</strong> Our Gas Safe registered engineers fit the boiler, flue, gas pipe and controls.</li>
        <li><strong>Day 5: clean, test, hand over.</strong> We clean the system, add inhibitor, fit the filter and balance each radiator. We show you the controls.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="paperwork">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>What paperwork and warranty do I get?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">You get the maker's boiler warranty, our 12-month workmanship guarantee, the Benchmark checklist and a Building Regulations certificate.</p>
      <p>We register the boiler warranty for you and email your documents the same day. The new boiler is notified to Building Control through the Gas Safe Register. Your certificate comes by post.</p>
      <p>Keep the warranty valid with a yearly <a href="/boiler-service-st-helens">boiler service</a>, £120 with us.</p>
      <h3>Landlords in St Helens</h3>
      <p>Newton-le-Willows and Earlestown have a growing number of rented homes. We fit central heating for landlords and can work with your tenant or agent. Rented homes need a <a href="/gas-safety-certificate-st-helens">gas safety certificate</a> every 12 months, from £100.</p>
      <h3>Which parts of St Helens do you cover?</h3>
      <div class="brx-table-wrap">
        <table class="brx-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Area</th><th>Places and postcodes</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><strong>St Helens town</strong></td><td>Town centre, Eccleston and Parr WA10. Sutton, Thatto Heath and Clock Face WA9.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Haydock and Rainford</strong></td><td>Haydock and Rainford WA11. Billinge WN5.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Newton-le-Willows</strong></td><td>Newton-le-Willows and Earlestown WA12. Golborne WA3.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div class="brx-danger"><p><strong>Smell gas?</strong> Call the National Gas Emergency line on 0800 111 999 first. Then call us.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</ServiceGuide>
